{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1177580-world-of-darkness-the-exigents","id":1177580,"title":"World of Darkness The Exigents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-20T07:17:47-08:00","id":1177580,"title":"World of Darkness The Exigents","content":"So an idea that simply crossed my mind, if you could make a circle of Exigents based on 5 splats from World of Darkness, what would they be? For the sake of simplicity, rolling Old, Chronicles and the God Machine into one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T07:41:03-08:00","id":1177587,"title":"","content":"So the thing is, Exigents are informed less by their domain than you might think. First and foremost, the thing determining what an Exigent is like is the <i>god</i>. You could have two &quot;Volcano Exigents&quot; who are nonetheless wildly different because one is the Chosen of a serpentine volcano-god of toxic fumes and slow creeping lava and one is the Chosen of a phoenix-like volcano-god of rare but explosive eruptions that nonetheless fertilize the land with ash for generations to come. So it's worth thinking about, not a vampire Exigent, but the Chosen of a specific powerful entity in vampire-lore and what they would be like.<br /> <br /> I know very little about the W/CofD beyond having read 2e Mage the Awakening, so I don't have specific thoughts to contribute, but I felt this was a point that should be made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T07:53:43-08:00","id":1177593,"title":"","content":"It works fairly well for vampires since their entire fluff is a progenitor that created all of them (OwoD) fluff. All the clans were made by older generation vampires, so technically most vampires copying the templates of their &quot;parents&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other gods to represent various splats could be possible of course, as there are many different kind of gods in creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T20:43:23-08:00","id":1177761,"title":"","content":"Its not World of Darkness, but the closest Splat I can think of might be Sion.<br /> <br /> The entire system is on the idea of &quot;a demi-god&quot; with a god &quot;parent&quot;. From there you gain powers based on &quot;fertility, chaos, fire, animals, etc...&quot; and that degree of variety while still within the restraints of a concept fit the idea of an Exigent.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping the Exigents fall towards this style - Charms based on their purviews of their God, instead of ability or attribute based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T17:36:19-08:00","id":1177969,"title":"","content":"I used an exigent as a major plot point in a story I ran over 7 sessions - he was very much based on the Hunters, as a kind of 'solar light' - very powerful within the domain of the god that created them, not so powerful out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}